[libs] Include pthread.h where pthread_once is used

pal_hmac.c uses pthread_once_t and PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT but includes neither
pthread.h nor anything that is guaranteed to pull it in - it relied on the
OpenSSL headers doing so. OpenSSL 3.5 no longer does, and the file stops
compiling:

    error: use of undeclared identifier 'PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT'
    error: call to undeclared function 'pthread_once'

Include it directly, as pal_evp.c, opensslshim.c and pal_bio.c in the same
library already do.

diff --git a/src/native/libs/System.Security.Cryptography.Native/pal_hmac.c b/src/native/libs/System.Security.Cryptography.Native/pal_hmac.c
index cb9ae46..6a7c54f 100644
--- a/src/native/libs/System.Security.Cryptography.Native/pal_hmac.c
+++ b/src/native/libs/System.Security.Cryptography.Native/pal_hmac.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 #include "pal_hmac.h"
 
 #include <assert.h>
+#include <pthread.h>
 
 static EVP_MAC* g_evpMacHmac = NULL;
 static pthread_once_t g_evpMacHmacInit = PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT;
